@startuml
title Enforce Subscription Limits - sequence diagram
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam wrapWidth 240
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #888888
  ParticipantBorderColor #444444
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

actor Customer as U
participant "View" as V <<View>> #EADCFF
participant OrderController as C <<Controller>> #D8F3DC
participant OrderService as S <<Service>> #DCECFF
participant ProductQuotaService as Q <<Service>> #DCECFF
participant ShopPlanClock as CK <<Service>> #DCECFF
participant ProductRepository as PR <<Repository>> #FFF1C9

== Checkout / order guard ==
U -> V : place order
V -> C : POST /api/orders/{userId}/batch
C -> S : makeOrders(userId, request)
S -> S : makeOrder(shop part) for each shop
loop each cart product (sorted by productId)
  S -> Q : requireAllowed(product)
  Q -> Q : allowed(product) = allowedIds([product]) contains product
  Q -> CK : now()
  CK --> Q : now
  Q -> Q : allowedSpecification(now): undeleted AND rank <= effective limit
  Q -> PR : findAll(allowedSpec AND id in ids, unpaged)
  PR --> Q : eligible ids
  alt product NOT in eligible ids
    Q --> S : 400 badRequest "Sản phẩm đang bị khóa do vượt giới hạn gói"
    S --> C : 400 order rejected
    C --> V : 400 error
    V --> U : show "Sản phẩm đang bị khóa do vượt giới hạn gói"
  else product allowed
    Q --> S : ok
    S -> S : continue normal order processing
  end
end

note over S
  Same guard runs in OrderService.previewVouchers (voucher preview), CartService,
  CustomerOrderService (3 call sites) and ShopPlanService.feature. It is a live check.
end note

ref over S, Q
  Creation guard (not requireAllowed): ManagerProductService.create calls
  ShopPlanService.assertCanCreate(shop) at 2 sites (create path, under the shop write lock).
  It reads the current subscription (forShop) and counts undeleted products (countForShop).
  If the count >= limit it throws 409 CONFLICT, otherwise it saves.
end ref

note over Q
  Effective limit: active Pro plan productLimit (null = unlimited),
  otherwise 5 for Free. Excess products are blocked, not deleted.
  Rank = createdDate, then id. CatalogService reuses allowedSpecification() and allowed().
end note

@enduml
